---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import Prose from '../../components/Prose.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  title="About — Luvita"
  description="Luvita is a software studio. We build our own products and take on select projects end to end."
  paths={{ tr: 'hakkimizda', en: 'about' }}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Software, done properly."
    lead="We are a software studio building software designed to last, and maintained like it matters."
  />

  <section class="container">
    <Prose>
      <p>
        Luvita is a software studio: we build products of our own and take on
        select projects end to end. We work with the rigor that banking and
        enterprise workflows demand: architecture decisions are documented,
        testing and automation are set up from day one, and every system we
        deliver stays under our care.
      </p>
      <p>
        Luvita is founder-led — every project is engineered end to end by the
        same hands that build our products. Our founder, <strong
        >Mert Yılmaz Ertuğrul</strong>, brings years of engineering
        experience in banking and enterprise software. Java/Spring Boot
        backend systems, cross-platform applications with Flutter, and cloud
        architectures are the studio's core competencies.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our consumer apps ship under the <strong>CosmoCrew</strong> brand —
        SliceFocus and LexiPower on the App Store, With Handlebars on the web.
        Taking software from idea to store and keeping it alive
        for years is the quality bar we bring to every engagement. Where we
        are headed is just as clear: growing platforms of our own — starting
        with <strong>Umay</strong>.
      </p>
      <h2>Our principles</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Transparency:</strong> scope, timeline and risks are shared
          openly at every stage.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Longevity:</strong> code is written for the team that reads
          it years later; docs and tests are first-class deliverables.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ownership:</strong> delivery is not an ending — it is the
          start of a long-term partnership.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
